282
00:10:52,707 --> 00:10:55,876
Electrek's third quarter to Cox's first two.

283
00:10:56,056 --> 00:10:58,331
Either way, that is less than the

284
00:10:58,331 --> 00:11:01,159
Nissan Frontier sold in the third quarter

285
00:11:01,159 --> 00:11:03,848
alone, which was twenty-three thousand,

286
00:11:03,848 --> 00:11:05,227
four hundred twelve.

287
00:11:05,578 --> 00:11:07,888
That comparison is not fair in one

288
00:11:07,888 --> 00:11:09,994
way, and it is important to say

289
00:11:09,994 --> 00:11:10,198
so.

290
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:13,315
The Cybertruck is a very different product,

291
00:11:13,315 --> 00:11:16,594
with a price near seventy-five thousand dollars,

292
00:11:16,594 --> 00:11:18,643
and it was never going to sell

293
00:11:18,643 --> 00:11:19,736
like a Maverick.

294
00:11:19,916 --> 00:11:22,471
A truck at that price competes with

295
00:11:22,471 --> 00:11:24,223
a small group of buyers.

296
00:11:24,403 --> 00:11:26,787
But the plan was two hundred fifty

297
00:11:26,787 --> 00:11:27,908
thousand a year,

298
00:11:27,908 --> 00:11:30,221
which is the size of a mainstream

299
00:11:30,221 --> 00:11:31,834
truck, not a niche one.

300
00:11:32,014 --> 00:11:34,373
That is where the gap comes from,

301
00:11:34,373 --> 00:11:36,160
and it is a gap between a

302
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:37,447
plan and a market,

303
00:11:37,447 --> 00:11:39,734
not between a truck and a truck.

304
00:11:40,085 --> 00:11:42,335
There is also a point about the

305
00:11:42,335 --> 00:11:45,021
electric truck rivals that is easy to

306
00:11:45,021 --> 00:11:45,530
forget.

307
00:11:45,710 --> 00:11:49,022
In the second quarter of twenty twenty-six,

308
00:11:49,022 --> 00:11:52,411
the Cybertruck sold more than the Lightning,

309
00:11:52,411 --> 00:11:54,953
the Silverado EV and the Rivian R

310
00:11:54,953 --> 00:11:55,416
one T.

311
00:11:55,596 --> 00:11:57,012
And the Lightning,

312
00:11:57,012 --> 00:11:59,215
which Ford stopped building,

313
00:11:59,215 --> 00:12:01,103
still sold two thousand,

314
00:12:01,103 --> 00:12:02,991
four hundred twenty-one.

315
00:12:03,171 --> 00:12:05,846
So demand for electric trucks exists,

316
00:12:05,846 --> 00:12:08,305
in the low thousands per truck per

317
00:12:08,305 --> 00:12:08,883
quarter.

318
00:12:09,063 --> 00:12:11,694
The question for every company is whether

319
00:12:11,694 --> 00:12:13,683
that is enough to build a truck

320
00:12:13,683 --> 00:12:13,939
for.

321
00:12:14,290 --> 00:12:15,961
What would change the picture?

322
00:12:16,141 --> 00:12:17,174
We do not know,

323
00:12:17,174 --> 00:12:19,032
and the sources do not say.

324
00:12:19,212 --> 00:12:22,504
Cheaper versions might bring in new buyers,

325
00:12:22,504 --> 00:12:25,566
as Tesla tried with the dual-motor truck

326
00:12:25,566 --> 00:12:26,178
in June.

327
00:12:26,358 --> 00:12:29,693
Gas prices might push buyers toward electric,

328
00:12:29,693 --> 00:12:32,435
as Electrek noted for the second half

329
00:12:32,435 --> 00:12:33,324
of the year.

330
00:12:33,504 --> 00:12:35,766
And the end of the federal tax

331
00:12:35,766 --> 00:12:38,781
credit has already removed one source of

332
00:12:38,781 --> 00:12:39,309
demand.

333
00:12:39,489 --> 00:12:40,905
Those are the forces,

334
00:12:40,905 --> 00:12:43,130
and the numbers in the next three

335
00:12:43,130 --> 00:12:45,422
quarters will show which one wins.

336
00:12:45,772 --> 00:12:46,682
For a buyer,

337
00:12:46,682 --> 00:12:48,732
the honest summary is this.

338
00:12:48,912 --> 00:12:51,180
The Cybertruck is a real truck,

339
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:53,521
with real owners and real sales.

340
00:12:53,701 --> 00:12:55,464
It is also a truck from a

341
00:12:55,464 --> 00:12:58,073
company that does not report how many

342
00:12:58,073 --> 00:13:00,118
it sells, in a market that is

343
00:13:00,118 --> 00:13:02,374
shrinking, at a price that rose.

344
00:13:02,554 --> 00:13:04,400
If you love the design and you

345
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:06,431
are comfortable with those facts,

346
00:13:06,431 --> 00:13:07,662
that is your choice.

347
00:13:07,842 --> 00:13:09,979
If you want the lowest risk,

348
00:13:09,979 --> 00:13:12,039
a truck with a long record,

349
00:13:12,039 --> 00:13:15,473
hundreds of thousands of owners and published

350
00:13:15,473 --> 00:13:17,304
numbers is a safer path.

351
00:13:17,655 --> 00:13:18,966
One last point.

352
00:13:19,146 --> 00:13:22,188
Reports like this one change every quarter.

353
00:13:22,368 --> 00:13:24,673
By the time you watch this video,

354
00:13:24,673 --> 00:13:26,768
new numbers may have come out.

355
00:13:26,948 --> 00:13:30,427
Check the latest quarter from Cox Automotive,

356
00:13:30,427 --> 00:13:33,287
and from Tesla's own delivery report.

357
00:13:33,467 --> 00:13:36,088
And remember that an estimate is an

358
00:13:36,088 --> 00:13:38,934
estimate, even when it appears in many

359
00:13:38,934 --> 00:13:39,458
places.

360
00:13:39,638 --> 00:13:41,579
The best habit is to look for

361
00:13:41,579 --> 00:13:43,587
the source, and to ask who has

362
00:13:43,587 --> 00:13:45,327
the data and who does not.

363
00:13:45,678 --> 00:13:48,719
So what is the Cybertruck problem?

364
00:13:48,899 --> 00:13:51,051
It is not that the truck failed

365
00:13:51,051 --> 00:13:52,092
to sell at all.

366
00:13:52,272 --> 00:13:54,865
Tesla sold tens of thousands in its

367
00:13:54,865 --> 00:13:57,532
best year, and it leads the electric

368
00:13:57,532 --> 00:14:00,198
pickups every quarter in the data we

369
00:14:00,198 --> 00:14:00,643
found.

370
00:14:00,823 --> 00:14:03,325
The problem is the gap between the

371
00:14:03,325 --> 00:14:04,724
plan and the sales.

372
00:14:04,904 --> 00:14:07,588
Two hundred fifty thousand a year was

373
00:14:07,588 --> 00:14:10,345
the plan, and about twenty thousand to

374
00:14:10,345 --> 00:14:13,101
thirty thousand a year is the reality,

375
00:14:13,101 --> 00:14:15,713
depending on whose estimate you use.

376
00:14:16,062 --> 00:14:18,494
And the problem is the wider electric

377
00:14:18,494 --> 00:14:19,348
truck market.

378
00:14:19,528 --> 00:14:23,370
The Silverado EV fell forty-three percent through

379
00:14:23,370 --> 00:14:24,311
nine months.

380
00:14:24,491 --> 00:14:26,837
The Lightning fell seventy-nine.

381
00:14:27,017 --> 00:14:29,455
The Hummer EV fell sixty-two.

382
00:14:29,635 --> 00:14:31,705
The Cybertruck is not alone,

383
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:33,849
and it is not even the worst.

384
00:14:34,029 --> 00:14:35,995
Its number is a symptom of a

385
00:14:35,995 --> 00:14:38,664
market that was planned for a subsidy,

386
00:14:38,664 --> 00:14:41,262
and that lost the federal tax credit.

387
00:14:41,442 --> 00:14:43,880
The truck that looks the most different

388
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,693
is in the same trouble as the

389
00:14:45,693 --> 00:14:47,944
ones that look like everything else.

390
00:14:48,294 --> 00:14:49,768
Before the checklist,

391
00:14:49,768 --> 00:14:52,928
let's turn the biggest numbers into something

392
00:14:52,928 --> 00:14:54,052
a buyer can use.

393
00:14:54,232 --> 00:14:56,901
Three different things have been mixed together

394
00:14:56,901 --> 00:14:57,866
in the headlines.

395
00:14:58,046 --> 00:15:00,149
A plan is what a company hopes

396
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:02,673
to sell, and for the Cybertruck that

397
00:15:02,673 --> 00:15:05,337
was two hundred fifty thousand a year.

398
00:15:05,517 --> 00:15:08,075
Capacity is what a factory is able

399
00:15:08,075 --> 00:15:11,234
to build, and the shareholder letter lists

400
00:15:11,234 --> 00:15:14,468
more than one hundred twenty-five thousand.

401
00:15:14,648 --> 00:15:17,864
Sales are what customers actually paid for.

402
00:15:18,044 --> 00:15:20,238
When you read a claim about any

403
00:15:20,238 --> 00:15:22,502
truck, ask which of the three it

404
00:15:22,502 --> 00:15:24,837
is, because mixing them up is the

405
00:15:24,837 --> 00:15:27,030
easiest way to end up confused.

406
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:30,213
Next, registrations and sales.

407
00:15:30,393 --> 00:15:33,004
A registration is a record that a

408
00:15:33,004 --> 00:15:35,931
truck is on the road under somebody's

409
00:15:35,931 --> 00:15:36,326
name.

410
00:15:36,506 --> 00:15:38,907
A sale is a customer choosing to

411
00:15:38,907 --> 00:15:39,432
buy it.

412
00:15:39,612 --> 00:15:41,782
We saw that S and P Global

413
00:15:41,782 --> 00:15:46,873
Mobility counted seven thousand and seventy-one registrations

414
00:15:46,873 --> 00:15:48,709
in the fourth quarter,

415
00:15:48,709 --> 00:15:51,380
while Cox counted four thousand,

416
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:53,383
one hundred forty sales,

417
00:15:53,383 --> 00:15:54,802
and one thousand,

418
00:15:54,802 --> 00:15:59,059
three hundred thirty-nine of the registrations went

419
00:15:59,059 --> 00:16:02,147
to SpaceX and Musk's other companies.

420
00:16:02,327 --> 00:16:03,906
The lesson is simple.

421
00:16:04,086 --> 00:16:07,123
Compare numbers only when they come from

422
00:16:07,123 --> 00:16:08,337
the same source,

423
00:16:08,337 --> 00:16:10,843
and always ask who the buyer was.

424
00:16:11,193 --> 00:16:13,595
Now think about the range between the

425
00:16:13,595 --> 00:16:16,711
two estimates, about thirty-seven hundred on one

426
00:16:16,711 --> 00:16:18,984
side and seven to eight thousand on

427
00:16:18,984 --> 00:16:19,633
the other.

428
00:16:19,813 --> 00:16:22,224
A buyer should read a wide range

429
00:16:22,224 --> 00:16:23,958
like that as a message.

430
00:16:24,138 --> 00:16:27,409
It says that nobody outside Tesla really

431
00:16:27,409 --> 00:16:27,899
knows.

432
00:16:28,079 --> 00:16:30,662
The lower figure is described as a

433
00:16:30,662 --> 00:16:34,309
low-confidence estimate, and the higher one uses

434
00:16:34,309 --> 00:16:36,891
Tesla's global total as a ceiling.

435
00:16:37,071 --> 00:16:39,202
Do not pick the number that supports

436
00:16:39,202 --> 00:16:40,682
what you already believe.

437
00:16:40,862 --> 00:16:42,502
Hold both in your head,

438
00:16:42,502 --> 00:16:44,926
and let the uncertainty be part of

439
00:16:44,926 --> 00:16:45,924
your decision.

440
00:16:46,274 --> 00:16:47,887
Then there is the price.

441
00:16:48,067 --> 00:16:51,619
The truck now starts at seventy-four thousand,

442
00:16:51,619 --> 00:16:54,707
nine hundred ninety dollars after a five

443
00:16:54,707 --> 00:16:56,637
thousand dollar increase,

444
00:16:56,637 --> 00:16:59,802
and the average full-size pickup sold for

445
00:16:59,802 --> 00:17:03,276
sixty-seven thousand, four hundred forty-six.

446
00:17:03,456 --> 00:17:05,562
A starting price is not what you

447
00:17:05,562 --> 00:17:05,825
pay.

448
00:17:06,005 --> 00:17:08,920
Ask for the out-the-door price in writing,

449
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:11,280
with every fee and every option on

450
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,390
the exact truck.

451
00:17:12,570 --> 00:17:14,866
Ask what day the quote is good

452
00:17:14,866 --> 00:17:17,621
for, because this price has moved in

453
00:17:17,621 --> 00:17:20,070
both directions in a short time.

454
00:17:20,250 --> 00:17:22,353
And if you compare it with another

455
00:17:22,353 --> 00:17:24,578
truck, compare the same kind of trim

456
00:17:24,578 --> 00:17:25,568
on the same day.

457
00:17:25,918 --> 00:17:28,049
Here is how to verify the truck

458
00:17:28,049 --> 00:17:28,530
itself.

459
00:17:28,710 --> 00:17:31,649
Take the vehicle identification number,

460
00:17:31,649 --> 00:17:33,985
the VIN, and run it through the

461
00:17:33,985 --> 00:17:36,848
official recall lookup before you pay.

462
00:17:37,028 --> 00:17:39,196
Ask for the service records,

463
00:17:39,196 --> 00:17:41,750
and ask for the warranty terms in

464
00:17:41,750 --> 00:17:43,994
writing, not in conversation.

465
00:17:44,174 --> 00:17:46,696
Then find out where the nearest service

466
00:17:46,696 --> 00:17:48,766
center is, and how long the wait

467
00:17:48,766 --> 00:17:50,188
is for an appointment.

468
00:17:50,368 --> 00:17:52,456
With a truck that has few sales

469
00:17:52,456 --> 00:17:54,207
and little published data,

470
00:17:54,207 --> 00:17:55,891
these checks matter more,

471
00:17:55,891 --> 00:17:58,518
because there are fewer owners who have

472
00:17:58,518 --> 00:18:00,875
already found the problems for you.

473
00:18:01,225 --> 00:18:02,764
Who is this truck for,

474
00:18:02,764 --> 00:18:04,163
and who should wait?

475
00:18:04,343 --> 00:18:06,456
It suits a buyer who loves the

476
00:18:06,456 --> 00:18:08,709
design, who has the budget for a

477
00:18:08,709 --> 00:18:11,597
price near seventy-five thousand dollars,

478
00:18:11,597 --> 00:18:14,907
and who is comfortable owning something unusual

479
00:18:14,907 --> 00:18:17,372
from a company that does not report

480
00:18:17,372 --> 00:18:18,217
its numbers.

481
00:18:18,397 --> 00:18:20,522
It may not suit a buyer who

482
00:18:20,522 --> 00:18:22,253
needs a proven record,

483
00:18:22,253 --> 00:18:23,985
who wants easy resale,

484
00:18:23,985 --> 00:18:26,660
or who depends on a nearby service

485
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:27,290
network.

486
00:18:27,470 --> 00:18:30,270
If that second description sounds like you,

487
00:18:30,270 --> 00:18:33,134
waiting for the next quarter's numbers costs

488
00:18:33,134 --> 00:18:35,218
very little, and it may tell you

489
00:18:35,218 --> 00:18:35,609
a lot.

490
00:18:35,959 --> 00:18:38,873
Finally, the mistakes we see most often.

491
00:18:39,053 --> 00:18:41,076
Buying because of a headline,

492
00:18:41,076 --> 00:18:43,449
either the one that says the truck

493
00:18:43,449 --> 00:18:45,542
failed or the one that says it

494
00:18:45,542 --> 00:18:45,961
leads.

495
00:18:46,141 --> 00:18:49,244
Forgetting that leading a small category is

496
00:18:49,244 --> 00:18:51,481
not the same as a large market.

497
00:18:51,661 --> 00:18:54,388
Paying the starting price without reading the

498
00:18:54,388 --> 00:18:54,691
fees.

499
00:18:54,871 --> 00:18:57,857
Skipping the recall check because the truck

500
00:18:57,857 --> 00:18:58,343
is new.

501
00:18:58,523 --> 00:19:01,345
And assuming that a company's confidence is

502
00:19:01,345 --> 00:19:03,248
the same as a company's data.

503
00:19:03,428 --> 00:19:06,114
A calm buyer with a written quote

504
00:19:06,114 --> 00:19:09,125
and a checked VIN is better protected

505
00:19:09,125 --> 00:19:10,752
than any prediction,

506
00:19:10,752 --> 00:19:11,892
ours included.

507
00:19:12,241 --> 00:19:14,544
To put all of this together,

508
00:19:14,544 --> 00:19:17,751
imagine you are standing in a showroom,

509
00:19:17,751 --> 00:19:20,136
or reading an online listing.

510
00:19:20,316 --> 00:19:22,631
Here is a short routine that works

511
00:19:22,631 --> 00:19:24,333
for any low-volume truck.

512
00:19:24,513 --> 00:19:27,526
First, write down the out-the-door price,

513
00:19:27,526 --> 00:19:30,539
and compare it with the average full-size

514
00:19:30,539 --> 00:19:32,817
pickup at sixty-seven thousand,

515
00:19:32,817 --> 00:19:35,095
four hundred forty-six dollars,

516
00:19:35,095 --> 00:19:37,447
so you know what the premium is.

517
00:19:37,627 --> 00:19:40,446
Second, ask for the warranty and service

518
00:19:40,446 --> 00:19:41,644
terms in writing.

519
00:19:41,824 --> 00:19:43,914
Third, run the VIN.

520
00:19:44,094 --> 00:19:47,313
Fourth, ask yourself which numbers you trust,

521
00:19:47,313 --> 00:19:48,958
and who published them.

522
00:19:49,138 --> 00:19:51,459
If you can answer all four calmly,

523
00:19:51,459 --> 00:19:53,097
you are ready to decide.

524
00:19:53,277 --> 00:19:54,168
If you cannot,

525
00:19:54,168 --> 00:19:56,332
the truck will still be there next

526
00:19:56,332 --> 00:19:56,714
month.

527
00:19:57,063 --> 00:19:59,530
So what should you check before you

528
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:00,728
buy a Cybertruck,

529
00:20:00,728 --> 00:20:02,420
or any low-volume truck,

530
00:20:02,420 --> 00:20:04,041
in twenty twenty-seven?

531
00:20:04,221 --> 00:20:05,906
First, the real price,

532
00:20:05,906 --> 00:20:07,055
with every fee,

533
00:20:07,055 --> 00:20:10,043
since the starting price has changed in

534
00:20:10,043 --> 00:20:11,268
both directions.

535
00:20:11,448 --> 00:20:14,822
Second, the warranty and the service network

536
00:20:14,822 --> 00:20:15,512
near you.

537
00:20:15,692 --> 00:20:17,750
Third, the resale value,

538
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:20,580
which the sources we found do not

539
00:20:20,580 --> 00:20:21,009
give.

540
00:20:21,189 --> 00:20:24,625
And fourth, the company's honesty about its

541
00:20:24,625 --> 00:20:25,264
numbers.

542
00:20:25,444 --> 00:20:27,944
A company that tells you how many

543
00:20:27,944 --> 00:20:30,065
it sells is easier to trust.

544
00:20:30,416 --> 00:20:32,142
We put all of this into a

545
00:20:32,142 --> 00:20:35,942
checklist, the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

546
00:20:36,122 --> 00:20:38,196
It covers the numbers to check,

547
00:20:38,196 --> 00:20:40,203
the questions to ask a dealer,

548
00:20:40,203 --> 00:20:42,879
and the warning signs we walked through.

549
00:20:43,059 --> 00:20:45,399
The link is in the description and

550
00:20:45,399 --> 00:20:46,913
in the pinned comment.

551
00:20:47,093 --> 00:20:49,605
If you want to know which engines

552
00:20:49,605 --> 00:20:51,509
to avoid in a used truck,

553
00:20:51,509 --> 00:20:54,477
subscribe, because that is coming soon.

554
00:20:54,657 --> 00:20:55,888
Thanks for watching.
